%li.dropdown
  - unless %w(users preferences partitions).include?(params[:controller])
    - count = current_user.partitions.count
    - if count > 0
      - if count > 1
        - current_partition = current_user.partition
        %a.dropdown-toggle{"data-toggle" => "dropdown", :href => "#"}
          %i.fa.fa-cube
          %span= current_partition.name
        %ul.dropdown-menu.dropdown-alerts
          %li
            - if count > 1
              = "You are assigned to #{count} partitions. You may change into another partition from here:"
            - else
              You are assigned to one partition. Please ask your administrator if this is incorrect.
          %li.divider
          %li
            - current_user.partitions.each do |partition|
              - if partition == current_partition
                %a{href: '#'}
                  %i.fas.fa-check-circle
                  = partition.name
              - else
                %a{href: main_app.user_change_partition_path(user_id: current_user.id, partition_id: partition.id)}
                  %i.far.fa-circle
                  = partition.name

    - else
      %a.dropdown-toggle{"data-toggle" => "dropdown", :href => "#"}
        %i.fa.fa-cube
        %span (Partition missing)
      %ul.dropdown-menu.dropdown-alerts
        %li
          You have to be assigned to at least one partition. Please ask your administrator if you can't fix this on your own.

  - else
    %a.dropdown-toggle{"data-toggle" => "dropdown", :href => "#"}
      %i.fa.fa-cube
      %span - Not applicable -
    %ul.dropdown-menu.dropdown-alerts
      %li
        %i.fa.fa-warning
        In this view, partitions are not applicable. If you move on to other non-system menus, selected partition will reappear.


